# NEXUS - Security Architecture

## 1. Security Principle
End-to-End Encryption is mandatory.

The server must never have access to plaintext private messages.

## 2. Encryption
- Use an audited E2EE protocol.
- No custom cryptographic algorithms.
- Encrypt messages on the sender's device.
- Decrypt messages only on authorized recipient devices.

## 3. Device Security
- Unique cryptographic identity per device.
- Device verification.
- Secure key storage.
- Session management.

## 4. File Security
- Encrypt files before uploading.
- Protect encryption keys separately.
- Never expose private file contents to the server.

## 5. Authentication
- Secure password hashing.
- Session protection.
- Rate limiting.
- Account recovery safeguards.

## 6. Privacy
- Minimize collected personal data.
- Avoid storing plaintext message content.
- No sensitive message content in push notifications.

## 7. Security Audits
- Dependency audits.
- Encryption implementation testing.
- Penetration testing.
- Vulnerability reporting.

## Status
Security requirements defined.
Implementation pending.
